{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Auto Test and Lint on Save",
  "description": "Automatically run tests and lint when TypeScript or JavaScript files are saved with minimal verbosity",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.jsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A JS/TS code file has been saved. Please:\n\n1. LINT: Run the project linter and formatter (ESLint, Prettier) using the project's existing config. Fix any auto-fixable issues and report remaining issues. Use commands like: npx eslint --fix <file>, npx prettier --write <file>.\n\n2. TEST: Run the appropriate tests for this file and report any failures. Use minimal verbosity to prevent session timeouts (--silent, --quiet flags). If this is a test file, run it directly with filtering (--grep, --testNamePattern). If this is a source file, find and run related tests. Use commands like: npm test -- --silent, npx jest --silent --testNamePattern='specific'."
  }
}